Tuuli Saarikoski wrote:
> I'm trying to get a Slash'EM wizard to survive at least until the Quest.
> She's chaotic, and human. Should she get an early wish, what should she wish
> for? Blessed +2 speed boots? SDSM? Perhaps something else?
>
> Seems to be pretty difficult to keep a wizard alive in Slash'EM's early
> levels.

SDSM is never a bad choice if survival is an issue, since you've
already got magic resistance, but remember you can take your pick of
DSM later when you hit the Wyrm caves.

Speed boots aren't bad either, but there's a pretty good chance of
stumbling across some elsewhere, and many people prefer WW-boots in [s]
anyway.

A +1 Helm of Brilliance is another good wish for an early wizard if
you've already got a (non-cursed) scroll of enchant armour or two. The
sooner you can cast those higher level spells the better you'll
survive. A HoB will up your AC nicely, protect you from rock traps and
improve your spellcasting. If you can get your HoB enchanted up enough
you may even find you can put on some mithril without nerfing your
(low-level) spellcasting rates too much.

If you have sleep or magic missile already, consider wishing for two
blessed potions of gain level. Quaff them when you're at full POW to
push up your maximum mana. If you're zapping sleep a lot, keeping your
levels low and letting your kitty do the killing (I've had quite a bit
of success playing the racket with [s] wizards) you'll be able to zap
sleep more or less indiscriminately, making life much easier for your
pet(s). If you're doing your own butchery, the added zap will be very
welcome when casting magic missile.

Slow digestion is another possibility to think about. IME wizards are
far more likely to make mid-game when they're not desperately
scrabbling around for food.

This might be contraversial, but if you can't find a co-aligned altar
anywhere (and you haven't already seen a load of artifacts), just go
ahead and wish for the blessed rustproof +2 magicbane. It makes such a
difference to a character's survivability, but sometimes you just can't
find an altar to sac for it.

Finally, I'll often blow an early wizard wish on a +2 cornuthaum, but
it might be that kind of decision making that has kept me from
ascending these last 3 years. 

Good luck, whatever you choose.



